    "description": "Loose sign heads, in front of shop wall and below the window sills. The upper edge has local steps by tenant, and several gaps behind tree trunks. The 2021 images show a different, pale continuous storefront installation. These samples concern alignment only."
  },
  "periods": {
    "2018": "Substantial cream stepped arch, four-light rectangular inner window and blue-green thin sheet, with weakly legible old plaque below.",
    "2022": "The 2021-01 street pair shows a new red scalloped canopy, additional top windows and red relief on the entrance face. The four-light rectangle remains visible under the canopy. The district article documents the later improved passage. This component retains the buried inner window only in its recent tower state; the newer surrounding work is constructed by the separate street-wall component.",
    "beyond_east_4": "At least one further broad curve and two narrower white heads are partly visible beyond the four measured openings (native u about 4140–4920). Both the existing dark awning and upper screen conceal the underlying glazing. They are not treated as further copies of the four measured sashes."
  },
